From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: schr-0dinger <kmkailasnath@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 21:08:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] imsservice: Apply the AOSP compat changes of
 samsung-ims-patches

The changes of the imsservice.apk imported with schr-0dinger's "update
vendor blobs and permissions for Samsung IMS support" (vendor b949f4d),
apart from those its rebuild made to every class (const-string/jumbo,
labels):

- Declare GoogleImsServiceAdapter as the compat ImsService (MMTEL
  feature, BIND_IMS_SERVICE), so that Android binds the stack.
- GoogleImsService reports the registration to Android: registered on
  LTE, voice, video and UT capabilities, onRegistered() callbacks.
- ImsServiceSwitchBase/ImsServiceSwitchEur: turn the IMS service
  switches on instead of reading Samsung's CSC.
- RJIL: P-CSCF from the link properties and UDP for SIP
  (RegistrationManagerBase, ResipRegistrationManager,
  RegistrationGovernorRjil), and its imsprofile.json entries.
- DmConfigHelper: answer the volte and mmtel DM config items.
- Drop Samsung-only code: Knox phone restriction policy (ImsUtil), HQM
  (ImsLogAgent), emergency and ultra power saving mode
  (ExternalSupporter, ImModule), MDEC (MdecAccountManager), NSDS
  multi-SIM service, RCS settings observers (RcsPolicyManager), and
  isProductShip() (Debug).
- Bundle imsmanager.jar's classes (com.sec.ims.*). Shared libraries
  are loaded ahead of the APK's own classes, so they are only used if
  imsmanager.jar is missing.
- Null checks in ConfigModule, GlobalSettingsRepo reading the SIM's
  carrier name from sys.smf.mnoname<n>, and smaller fixes in
  GlobalSettingsInternal, ImPersister, ImsAutoUpdate, ImsProfileCache,
  RegistrationGovernorImpl, StackIF, ServiceStateWrapper,
  TelephonyManagerWrapper and VolteServiceModule.

Assisted-by: LLM
